  "title": "OpenBMI SSVEP EEG dataset (Lee et al. 2019)",
  "description": "A BIDS-formatted derivative dataset of steady-state visually evoked potential (SSVEP) EEG recordings from 54 subjects across 2 sessions. This dataset comprises 21,600 trials of 4-second EEG recordings at 1000 Hz sampling frequency from 62 channels, organized for standardized brain-computer interface benchmarking. The data has been processed and converted to BIDS format using the Mother of All BCI Benchmarks (MOABB) framework, enabling reproducible analysis of SSVEP-based BCI paradigms with 4 stimulus classes.",
